<LegalLayout title="Privacy — Kuchi">
  <h1>Kuchi privacy</h1>
  <p>Updated November 13, 2026. Kuchi is Kalaris Labs’ collection of launch-video references.</p>
  <h2>No accounts</h2>
  <p>Kuchi has no accounts and no sign-in. You can browse the collection, play videos and connect an agent to the MCP server without giving us your name, email address or any other account information. Kuchi does not accept uploads.</p>
  <h2>Your agent and service providers</h2>
  <p>Agents connect to Kuchi’s MCP server without credentials. Its tools return reference videos, their measurements and remake plans. When your agent asks Kuchi to plan or check a remake, it sends details of your product (its name, description, features, on-screen copy and a description of your assets). Kuchi uses them to answer that one request and does not store them or send them to analytics. Your agent provider handles your conversations under its own privacy policy; Kuchi does not receive them.</p>
  <p>Cloudflare hosts the website, the videos and the MCP service. It processes request information, including IP addresses, to deliver the service and prevent abuse (requests are rate-limited per IP address; for this we keep only a count of recent requests, deleted after about an hour without requests). Operational logs may include request times, paths and errors.</p>
  <h2>Product analytics</h2>
  <p>We use PostHog, hosted in the United States, to understand how Kuchi is used. Analytics requests go through this site’s own <code>/relay</code> path.</p>
  <p><strong>On the website</strong> we record page views, clicks on buttons and links, reference viewing, filter use (how long a search is and how many results it gave, never the words), connection attempts, page performance and script errors. Nothing is stored in your browser for this: no cookies and no local storage, so each visit is counted on its own and we cannot recognize you when you return. We do not record sessions or what you type. Your IP address is used to deliver the request and is not saved with the event; we keep only the country reported by Cloudflare. Analytics are switched off completely when your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control.</p>
  <p><strong>On the MCP server</strong> we record which tool ran, how long it took, whether it failed, the name and version of the connecting client, its country, the catalog search terms and filters used, which reference was requested, and a one-line description of the task if the agent chooses to send one. We do not record your product details, the plans Kuchi returns, or IP addresses. If an agent uses the feedback tool, we store the note it writes.</p>
  <p>None of this is linked to a name, an email address or an account, because Kuchi has none.</p>
  <p data-web-only>If you pick light or dark mode, your browser remembers that choice in local storage on your device. It is never sent to us or to analytics.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or removal requests: <a href="mailto:support@kalarislabs.com">support@kalarislabs.com</a>.</p>
  <p><a href="/">Back to the collection ↗</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
